{
    "background_story": "Miles was a brilliant mathematician with a fascination for geometry. He spent most of his career studying the intricacies of tangency, the point where two curves touch but don't intersect. His colleagues often joked that Miles's life was a tangent to the rest of the world, as he was always slightly detached, observing life from a unique angle. Despite this, Miles's work had a profound impact on the field of mathematics, particularly in the study of circles and spheres. His groundbreaking research on tangent lines and circles led to breakthroughs in fields such as physics and engineering. Miles's love for tangency extended beyond mathematics; he believed that the concept represented the human experience \u2013 moments of connection and understanding that, though fleeting, leave a lasting impact.",
